## 3. Decisions & Rationale

- **A bare filename is legal when its folder already states the context.**
  `file-structure.md` §1.1 documents `components/ComponentFoo.tsx` — a component is named for
  the component, not a role or its folder — so the rule allows a bare name inside a grouping
  folder (`components`, `utils`, `tests`). That list is extracted to `rules/constants.ts` and
  read by both this rule and `no-misnamed-primary-file`, which had the same list inline.
  Without it the tighten produced 187 false positives, almost all component files.
- **`src/` was not role-conforming, and `no-ad-hoc-file-suffix` could not tell.** Its
  extension-only pattern accepted any bare name, so `references.ts` passed while stating no
  role. That is why 0.1–0.3 could not be verified from a green lint, and why the bare-name
  ban is the change that makes "role file" a decidable question.
- **The `Word/` folder collapses.** `wordGroups.ts`, `getAnagramKey.ts` and
  `getPossibleWords.ts` are all the `utils` role, so §1.2's `Feature.utils.ts` expresses them
  as one file exporting a single grouped value. `constants.ts` has five bare consts and
  becomes `Word.constants.ts`. Consolidating now satisfies Step 1 rather than renaming and
  rediscovering it: a `utils` file exporting two values is exactly what `no-multiple-exports`
  flags, and `getPossibleWords.ts` exporting `transformAnagramMap` is a name the file does
  not define. `Types/Level.ts` and `Types/Words.ts` fold the same way into `Word.types.ts`.
- **`LocalSession.ts` is the session's slice of `localStorage`, so it stays with Session.**
  It shares `APP_KEY` with `App.provider.tsx` and mirrors `WordDuelArena`'s device-id slice,
  so the folder is right and only the role was missing — `Session.repository.ts`, §1.2's
  "data access". Moving it to `common/` would put session knowledge in shared code. The three
  slices reimplementing "read my key, update my slice" is a `/generalise` candidate.
- **`src/router.tsx` is a routes file, not an entry point** — it exports `routes` and
  `router`, and §1.2's `Feature.routes.tsx` is documented as a keyed map plus a derived
  array, so two exports is the shape. Renamed `src/router.routes.tsx`.
- **`extends Document` must carry its id type.** Twelve `*.types.ts` interfaces still
  declare `extends Document` with no argument, which makes `_id` `any` and trips five
  `no-unsafe-*` rules at every `_id` read. `server/App/Users/Users.types.ts` is the one
  fixed so far, and it took `server/App/Users` from 10 errors to 0. `.github/skills/db/`
  carries the defect too, so the `db` skill teaches it and should be corrected with them.
  The remainder are latent rather than live — they only report where a caller reads `_id`.
- **`no-ad-hoc-file-suffix` gained `service`, `middlewares` and `**/\*.d.ts`as exclusions
or roles** rather than renaming files.`file-structure.md`§2.1 documents`Feature.middlewares.ts`as plural, so the rule was out of step with the doc. A
declaration file's name describes what it augments, not a role, so`.d.ts` leaves scope.
- **`no-unused-vars` needed an ignore pattern, not nine edits.** `@typescript-eslint`'s
  replacement for the core rule honours no `_` convention by default, unlike the ESLint
  original — which is why the project's own deliberate-unused marker was reported.
- **`no-base-to-string` fires on an `object` narrowing.** Where a guard has narrowed to
  bare `object`, `object` carries `Object.prototype.toString`; naming a
  `{ toString(): string }` binding, or narrowing straight from `unknown`, satisfies it.
  `Predicate.isObjectId` and `ApiTransformers.toApiValue` both needed this.
- **`Repository`'s `ModelLike` is generic over the document type.** Threading `D` through
  `makeCrud` removed four `as Promise<…>` casts that the type-aware pass saw through.
  No mongoose coupling was added, so `0004`'s duck-typed design stands.
- Step 0 absorbs the `server/` and `common/` lint debt rather than the debt
  becoming a separate ticket. Measured at 124 errors; only 23 are this ticket's
  own rules. The remainder is fixed properly — the `no-unsafe-*` boundary types
  are resolved rather than cast quiet, because a cast that satisfies the linter
  while leaving `any` in place contradicts `no-unnecessary-type-assertion` in the
  same run.
- The lint script widened from `eslint src` to `eslint src server common`, and
  `server/**` left the top-level `ignores`. Both were required: a CLI path filter
  cannot be widened by config, and a config `files` glob cannot reach a file the
  CLI never selected. The ignore alone changed nothing — the script was the gate
  that mattered.
- `no-ad-hoc-file-suffix` is the right home for the bare-source ban. The rule
  already owns "is this filename legal?" and a bare `.ts` is currently legal by
  omission, not by decision — the extension-only pattern accepts any name.
  Widening its scope to `server/` is what made 23 accumulated violations visible
  for the first time.
- `rules/readme.md` now documents the shipped `RuleRegistrar` shape — folder,
  entry, field table — after months of describing a `title` / `rationale` /
